quint-check bundles no third-party code. It runs these dependencies, which are
installed separately and keep their own licenses:

- Quint (@informalsystems/quint, https://github.com/quint-co/quint),
  Apache License 2.0: its frontend produces the IR quint-check translates.
- tla-ts (https://github.com/aidenybai/tla-ts), MIT: it checks the TLA+
  quint-check produces.

conformance/public/ holds Quint models copied unchanged from Quint's examples
(https://github.com/quint-co/quint/tree/07d7a1a69c2093b5bc656caf3b5dfefa0d766cd0/examples),
by Quint's authors (its source files name Informal Systems), Apache License 2.0:
booleans.qnt, instances.qnt, weakFairness.qnt, coin.qnt, ewd426_3.qnt,
ewd426_4.qnt, two_phase_commit.qnt, tictactoe.qnt, BinSearch.qnt, generate.qnt,
counters.qnt, bakery.qnt, play_rock_paper_scissors.qnt, ewd426.qnt, ewd840.qnt,
prisoners.qnt, DiningPhilosophers5.qnt, tuples.qnt,
games/secret-santa/secret_santa.qnt and spells/basicSpells.qnt.

The conformance harness also runs, when present, Apalache
(https://github.com/apalache-mc/apalache, Apache License 2.0), which Quint
downloads. The translator
was written against Apalache's Quint converter as a reference for Quint's
operators; no code was copied from it.
